# Telemetry partitions merge as a UNION. A partition is append-only JSONL — one
# event per line, every line independent and self-timestamped — so when the same
# partition file name exists on two branches, `keep every line of both` is the
# correct resolution and git can reach it with no human in the loop.
#
# Without this, one name on two branches CONFLICTS: `CONFLICT (content)` when the
# branches share a base and both appended, `CONFLICT (add/add)` when the two copies
# have no shared base at all. Branches that touch DIFFERENT partition names merge
# cleanly either way — union is not what makes the ordinary case work. It is the
# net under the case where one name acquires two writers, which redkiln has shipped
# as a bug once already (its issue #64).
#
# Scoped to telemetry, never a blanket `*.jsonl`: union resolves SILENTLY, which is
# only ever right for an append-only log. Anywhere else it fabricates a file that
# neither side wrote.
telemetry/**/*.jsonl merge=union
